  "result": "I've written the plan but haven't changed any code. I couldn't submit it for approval because the plan-approval tool isn't available in this session. Plan mode is still active, so please tell me to go ahead if you want me to implement it.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py:603` uses `shlex.shlex`, which treats `#` as a comment character by default. Everything after a `#` is dropped, so `cli a #b c` loses `#b c`. In Fish, an incomplete word starting with `#` also raises `IndexError`. All four shells split their words through this one function, so they all have the problem.\n\n**Plan** (also saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-delegated-cray.md`):\n1. Set `lex.commenters = \"\"` in `split_arg_string`, with a short comment explaining why.\n2. Add a `versionchanged` note to its docstring and an entry in `CHANGES.rst`.\n3. Add tests in `tests/test_shell_completion.py`:\n   - a direct unit test of `split_arg_string`: `\"a #b c\"`, `\"foo#bar\"` and `\"a '#b\"` (incomplete quote);\n   - `#` cases in `test_full_complete` for bash and fish.\n4. Run `tests/test_shell_completion.py` and then the full suite. I'll also check that the new tests fail without the fix.",
